Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"tom|A text from TNB.":"","tom|\"Also there are acorns in the flour.\"":"","tom|I did not picture acorns.":"","tom|He has a key. I gave him a key for exactly this kind of emergency.":"","tom|...Where is Bready Mercury.":"","tnb|Okay. Hi. Love you. Do not panic. Look at the island.":"","tnb|That is the thing. I came over to feed him, like you asked. The jar was gone. The window was open.":"","tnb|And there were tiny footprints in the flour. Four toes in front, five in back. I looked it up.":"","tom|Bready Mercury is nine years old. He has flown Delta One. Twice.":"","tom|Somebody took my starter. And left a calling card.":"","tnb|And this was on the windowsill. An acorn. With a tiny X carved in it.":"","tnb|I know, babe. I have seen every horror movie ever made. This is exactly how they start.":"","tom|Nara is scared of the vacuum. Nara does not growl at trees.":"","tnb|Exactly. Something is going on out there.":"","tnb|Olivia texted me too. Nara has not slept in three days. She just stands at the window and growls at trees.":"","olivia|Tom! Oh, thank goodness. Can you take her? Please? She has not slept since Sunday.":"","michael|I found my car keys in the gutter. With three peanuts. Arranged in a triangle.":"","tnb|A triangle. Babe. A triangle is a SYMBOL.":"","tom|TNB has seen a lot of movies.":"","tom|Nara. Want to go for a walk?":"","olivia|Bernadette from the Neighborhood Watch says it is squirrels. She has a clipboard about it. She is in Old Oak Park, at the south end of 2nd Ave.":"","olivia|Bring her back tired! Please! Michael, can you grab Isla? She is licking the mailbox.":"","penny|Halt. Neighborhood Watch. State your business.":"","tom|Tom. 3468. I have lived on 2nd Ave for six years.":"","penny|I know who you are. You water your drought garden. Everybody knows.":"","penny|The squirrels are organized.":"","penny|Bernadette. Neighborhood Watch Captain, nineteen years. And I will say it, because nobody else will.":"","tnb|I KNEW it.":"","penny|Lookouts in the playground. A spy in the community garden. Somebody at the picnic tables stuffing their cheeks with anything that is not nailed down.":"","penny|And it all goes up THAT tree. The Old Oak. There is a little door in the trunk. I have heard a secret knock. Only bits of it.":"","tom|They buried something. Three somethings.":"","penny|Clear out those lookouts and your dog can dig. I will be here. With my clipboard.":"","tnb|Babe, she has a corkboard with red string. I have never felt so seen.":"","toad|BOO! BOOOO! Get off the stage! This is OUR playground!":"","tnb|Is it heckling us? From inside a peanut?":"","toad|Your shoes are untied! Made you look! BOOOO!":"","tom|My shoes do not have laces.":"","tnb|The playground is clear. And Nara is staring at the sandbox like it owes her money.":"","skeeter|...You did not see me. I am a stick. Sticks do not talk.":"","skeeter|Standard issue. Code name: Twig. I report to the Chairman. Pretend I said nothing.":"","tom|The Chairman.":"","tnb|That stick has binoculars.":"","tom|The garden is clear. Every tomato has exactly one bite out of it. That is a policy.":"","mudling|Mmmf. Mmmf mmf! (These are MY sandwiches.)":"","tom|Those are somebody’s sandwiches. Somebody’s whole birthday picnic.":"","mudling|Mmf. (Winter is coming. Winter is ALWAYS coming.)":"","tnb|Buddy. It is Los Angeles. It is seventy-four degrees.":"","tnb|The picnic is clear. The cake survived. The cake is a hero.":"","tom|Eleven tennis balls. Those are Marisol’s.":"","tnb|That is all three scraps. One acorn, two acorns, three acorns. It is a sequence, babe. It is ALWAYS a sequence.":"","tom|A pair of reading glasses. Those are Mr. Washington’s.":"","tom|One acorn: TAP TAP. Two acorns: SCRATCH. Three acorns: CHITTER.":"","tnb|We bring them back today. Personally. With a pastry.":"","tom|Mr. Washington reads the paper on his porch every morning. He has been reading the same headline for three days.":"","tom|A little yellow toy truck. Those are Lachlan’s.":"","tnb|And there is a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of three acorns. And one word: CHITTER.":"","tnb|And there is a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of one acorn. And one word: TAP TAP.":"","tom|Tom always keeps a heel of sourdough in his jacket. For emergencies. This is an emergency.":"","tnb|She has not eaten in three days, and she just ate your emergency bread.":"","tom|Yes.":"","tom|It lied to me first. It said it was an acorn.":"","tom|She will only eat bread if I throw it. Still true. Still very picky. Still very athletic.":"","tnb|Babe. You lied to a squirrel.":"","tom|Then we stay together.":"","tom|He is up there. And there is no ladder.":"","tnb|Babe. Babe. They have a corkboard. With RED STRING. I have waited my whole life for this.":"","tom|We need about forty pounds.":"","tnb|...":"","tom|Nara. Sit. In the bucket.":"","tom|Very brave. Extremely brave. You will be getting a lot of chicken.":"","tnb|Babe. Look. On top of the pile.":"","tom|BREADY MERCURY!":"","bigone|ORDER. ORDER! Who let a DOG into the Oak?":"","tom|It is Los Angeles. Winter is a light jacket.":"","bigone|That is what they WANT you to think.":"","tom|That is Bready Mercury. He is nine. You feed him flour and water, and then you SHARE the bread. That is the whole point of him.":"","bigone|I am the Chairman. Chairman Cheeks. Every acorn, every peanut, every shiny thing on 2nd Avenue comes up this tree. Because winter is coming.":"","bigone|And this jar. This jar smells like bread FOREVER. You feed it and it grows. It never runs out. It is the perfect hoard.":"","tom|Put the starter down. No touching, please.":"","tnb|Okay. Shake it off. Everybody gets a snack.":"","tom|Hello, Bready Mercury. Did you miss me? You were on an adventure.":"","tom|You are going to be extremely sour about this.":"","bigone|Fine. FINE. This meeting is adjourned. I am going to go stare at a bird feeder.":"","tom|He is a starter. Sour is a compliment.":"","tnb|Was that a pun? Babe. Did you just make a PUN?":"","tom|The sundial. The steamer. The sign-up sheet. Now my jar. Somebody keeps leaving these where we will find them.":"","olivia|Tom! You found everything! Marisol’s balls, Mr. Washington’s glasses, Lachlan’s truck. He has not put it down. He is eating cereal with one hand.":"","tom|Squirrels hoard shiny things. Squirrels do not tape things. Look at those corners.":"","tnb|Somebody in a long coat, if your niece and your kettle are right. Spooky. I love it. I hate it.":"","penny|Neighborhood Watch Captain’s report: case closed.":"","penny|I would like it noted that I was right.":"","tnb|Noted. On a corkboard. With red string.":"","michael|Lachlan wants Nara to have this. He painted a tennis ball gold. It took him four days and most of a bottle of paint.":"","tnb|You know what today was, babe? Absolutely nuts.":"","penny|And these. Neighborhood Watch Vests. I give out one every nineteen years. Today I am giving out three. Even the dog.":"","tom|...That is not a pun. That is just a word.":"","tnb|It is a word with a pun in its heart.":"","tom|A text from Grace. \"TATA. The library is WHISPERING. Like actually. Page says it is fine. It is NOT fine. Come home.\"":"","tom|Fine. It was nuts.":"","tnb|The library is whispering. Is that not just... its job?":"","tom|Not on Long Island. On Long Island, the library shushes YOU.":"","olivia|Thank you, Tom. Tell TNB thank you. Tell the squirrels nothing.":"","olivia|Is she okay? Is she eating? She is not eating, is she.":"","olivia|Michael, the squirrel is back on the fence. Do not make eye contact.":"","michael|Lachlan got his truck back. He has not put it down. He is eating cereal with one hand.":"","michael|I have both kids and zero car keys. Wait. Keys. Gutter. Right.":"","washington|Back in 1979 the squirrels were polite. They waited until you finished your sandwich.":"","washington|My reading glasses! Found in a hole in the park. I will not ask.":"","washington|Somebody took my reading glasses off the porch rail. I have read the same headline for three days.":"","olivia|Nara slept! Twelve hours! She is snoring like Michael.":"","la_woman|Eleven tennis balls! Back! My dog is beside himself. Wherever he is.":"","washington|I think it says WEATHER. It might say WHETHER.":"","gus|I am blowing leaves. The squirrels keep blowing them back.":"","la_woman|There he is. No. That is a squirrel. It is looking at me.":"","gus|It is a whole system. Their system is better.":"","penny|Case closed. I have filed my report. With myself. I approved it.":"","penny|You are a good neighbor, Tom. So is the dog. Mostly the dog.":"","la_woman|Every tennis ball on the block. Gone. My dog has nothing to ignore now.":"","penny|The lookouts first. Playground, garden, picnic tables. Then that dog of yours digs.":"","penny|Then the tree. There is a knock. I have only ever heard parts of it.":"","penny|Except squirrels. I am working on it.":"","skeeter|I am just an acorn. With sunglasses. That is all you need to know.":"","penny|Bernadette. Neighborhood Watch Captain, nineteen years. Nothing gets past me.":"","skeeter|The Chairman sees everything. Mostly from the tree.":"","penny|I said they were organized. Nobody believed me. Write that down.":"","skeeter|Agents, regroup!":"","skeeter|Round 2. Over.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Over.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Over.":"","skeeter|You did not see me. I was never here.":"","mudling|Everybody touches the tree and then says EW. I am the tree.":"","mudling|I am not sticky. I am committed.":"","mudling|Round 2. Stickier.":"","mudling|Round 3. Stickier.":"","mudling|Round 5. Stickier.":"","mudling|...Ooze. Ooze.":"","mudling|Round 4. Stickier.":"","mudling|Give me a hundred years. I will be amber.":"","toad|Nobody ever cheers for the peanut. They just crack us open.":"","toad|I boo because nobody ever asks what I think.":"","toad|Boo! Round two!":"","toad|Round 2. Still booing.":"","toad|Round 4. Still booing.":"","toad|Round 5. Still booing.":"","toad|Round 3. Still booing.":"","toad|...Boo. Quietly. Boo.":"","toad|I have notes. I always have notes.":"","skeeter|Code name: Twig. I report to the Chairman. Pretend I said nothing.":"","skeeter|Back on the stakeout!":"","mudling|Still oozing!":"","skeeter|Round 2. Still watching.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Still watching.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Still watching.":"","skeeter|...I am a stick.":"","skeeter|Report to the Chairman: they are very tall.":"","mudling|Mmmf. (Winter is coming. Winter is ALWAYS coming.)":"","mudling|Mmf mmf mmf. (Nobody ever shares with a squirrel.)":"","mudling|Mmmf! Round two!":"","skeeter|Nobody looks twice at a stick. That is the job. It is lonely.":"","mudling|Round 2. Mmf.":"","mudling|Round 3. Mmf.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Still watching.":"","mudling|Round 4. Mmf.":"","mudling|...Mmmf.":"","mudling|Mmf mmf. (Winter is coming.)":"","skeeter|...":"","bigone|Every shiny thing on 2nd Avenue comes up this tree. Because winter is coming.":"","mudling|Round 5. Mmf.":"","bigone|Nobody shares with a squirrel. So the squirrel takes.":"","bigone|ORDER! Round two!":"","bigone|Round 2. Meeting is still in session.":"","bigone|Round 3. Meeting is still in session.":"","bigone|Round 4. Meeting is still in session.":"","bigone|Round 5. Meeting is still in session.":"","bigone|Winter is coming. Write that down.":"","bigone|...Order. Order.":"","sal|Airport? You JUST landed. Your young man called the depot. Something about your bread.":"","sal|He said, and I quote, \"tell him it is a bread emergency.\" I did not know bread could have those.":"","skeeter|...It is an acorn.":"","tom|\"Babe. Come home. Your house. NOW. It is about Bready Mercury.\"":"","skeeter|I said NOTHING.":"","tnb|Okay. Shake it off. Everybody gets a snack and a hug. In that order.":"","olivia|That. All night. And it is not just us. Lachlan’s toy truck is gone. Mr. Washington’s reading glasses. Marisol says every tennis ball on the block.":"","tnb|And there is a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of two acorns. And one word: SCRATCH.":"","tnb|That is what they always say in the second act.":"","tnb|Babe. We are inside a tree. This is the second act of every horror movie I have ever seen.":"","tom|That is my house. That is my JAR. Why is my jar in the middle of everything?":"","tnb|Everything connects to the jar, babe. That is how corkboards work.":"","tnb|It is a counterweight. Put enough weight in the bucket and the ladder comes down. Classic pulley.":"","tnb|It is a squirrel in a tiny tie, babe. I am so scared and so delighted.":"","bigone|Share? ...Nobody shares. Not with a squirrel. Twenty years, and every bird feeder on the block has chased me off it.":"","tnb|Babe, when it buries an acorn, break it before it eats it. Nara digs them up for double. And maybe... share something with it. Three times.":"","tnb|And look. Something taped to the lid. A gold coin. With a little clock face.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Over.":"","skeeter|...Copy that. Over.":""});
